# Example events/*.json bridge target - see events/example_deep_mining_guard.json.
#
# Demonstrates BlockBreakWrapper's typed properties (event.block, event.player, event.drop_items/
# event.exp_to_drop) instead of the generic BukkitEvent reflective wrapper example.pf uses. With the
# generic wrapper this would be event.get("block")/event.get("player") - every key is a bare string
# with no compile-time (or even load-time) checking, so a typo like "drop_item" instead of
# "drop_items" would silently read back NULL forever instead of failing loudly, and the returned
# value still needs manual type coercion before it's usable. The dedicated wrapper's properties are
# real PolyType members: a typo is a script-parse-time "unknown property" error, and event.block
# comes back as an already-wrapped Block object (block.pos.y, block.id, ...) with no reflection or
# coercion step in between.
# The guard line is set to -1000 - below the bottom of any real world (min build height is -64) -
# so this example doesn't silently break normal mining/building on a fresh install. Raise it (e.g.
# to 5) only if you actually want a deep-mining guard; y<=5 covers nearly the entire underground of
# a modern world and will make it look like block-breaking is broken server-wide.
def on_break():
    if event.block.pos.y <= -1000:
        # Below the "deep guard" line: refuse the break outright and tell the player why. cancel()
        # is the same Event.cancel() every wrapper shares, but block/player here are typed objects,
        # not reflectively-fetched values, so there's nothing to coerce before using them.
        event.cancel()
        Player.send_message("<red>Mining this deep is off-limits here.")
    else:
        # Above the line: let the break happen, but reward it - double the vanilla XP orb this
        # block would have dropped. set_exp_to_drop/exp_to_drop are real typed accessors, not a
        # generic event.get("expToDrop")/event.set("expToDrop", ...) round-trip.
        event.set_exp_to_drop(event.exp_to_drop * 2)
    end
end
